{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00177",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 4.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Morning. Nice to finally see you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.56,
      "end_seconds": 8.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.45,
      "end_seconds": 15.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Um, honestly, it's aching in my thighs, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.83,
      "end_seconds": 20.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.09,
      "end_seconds": 24.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "It's been five days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.68,
      "end_seconds": 28.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Alright, does anything bring it on or make it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.96,
      "end_seconds": 31.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I notice it more with climbing stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.46,
      "end_seconds": 35.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.26,
      "end_seconds": 42.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Weakness getting out of a chair goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.54,
      "end_seconds": 48.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "So, any trouble swallowing, joint swelling or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.46,
      "end_seconds": 51.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.7,
      "end_seconds": 54.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.79,
      "end_seconds": 59.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Amlodipine. I take it 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.39,
      "end_seconds": 65.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.41,
      "end_seconds": 73.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.33,
      "end_seconds": 92.04,
      "duration_seconds": 16.71,
      "text": "Go on. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.7,
      "end_seconds": 94.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.0,
      "end_seconds": 101.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.02,
      "end_seconds": 102.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.41,
      "end_seconds": 107.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.46,
      "end_seconds": 121.55,
      "duration_seconds": 12.09,
      "text": "Uh, yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.84,
      "end_seconds": 125.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.65,
      "end_seconds": 128.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.51,
      "end_seconds": 133.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.6,
      "end_seconds": 135.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.57,
      "end_seconds": 138.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.16,
      "end_seconds": 158.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Power in the thighs is slightly reduced, four out of five."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.86,
      "end_seconds": 162.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.58,
      "end_seconds": 175.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "The muscles are mildly tender when I squeeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.98,
      "end_seconds": 177.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.48,
      "end_seconds": 192.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.19,
      "end_seconds": 196.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.37,
      "end_seconds": 226.34,
      "duration_seconds": 16.97,
      "text": "Okay, continuing. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.65,
      "end_seconds": 232.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.56,
      "end_seconds": 251.82,
      "duration_seconds": 18.26,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had aching in your thighs for five days, and no numbness or joint swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.23,
      "end_seconds": 253.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.13,
      "end_seconds": 257.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.79,
      "end_seconds": 262.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.55,
      "end_seconds": 289.67,
      "duration_seconds": 26.12,
      "text": "Let's get a creatine kinase level, for muscle pain. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Don't stop any of your tablets on your own, we'll decide after the blood test. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.43,
      "end_seconds": 293.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.24,
      "end_seconds": 297.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.91,
      "end_seconds": 305.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.36,
      "end_seconds": 309.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "So, I come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.54,
      "end_seconds": 315.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Right, yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.07,
      "end_seconds": 318.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}